When cosmic-comp exits before it is ready (no display, no usable GPU),
cosmic-session waits for its environment forever: the exit is reported on
the session channel, which is only read once the session is up. The
desktop never comes back to the login screen and the user sees nothing.
Watch the channel while waiting, and exit with an error instead (a
restart would fail the same way) so the greeter can show the log.
Applied to cosmic-session by tools/dev/cosmic-build.sh patch.
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -108,6 +108,12 @@
 			Ok(Status::Restarted) => {
 				info!("Restarting");
 			}
+			Ok(Status::Failed) => {
+				// Restarting would only fail the same way, so fail the session.
+				return Err(color_eyre::eyre::eyre!(
+					"the compositor exited before it was ready"
+				));
+			}
 			Err(error) => {
 				error!("Restarting after error: {:?}", error);
 			}
